# ~/.vct-secrets/shared/ — shared-scope secret keys

Each regular file in this directory is ONE secret: the file name is the key
(and, by convention, the env-var name it maps to when injected via
`vct exec --secret KEY=ENV_VAR`). Files are mode 600; this directory is 700.

Managed by the `vct` CLI (`tools/vct-secrets/vct` in the orchestrator repo):

```bash
vct list                          # key names only, never values
vct can-read --key KEY            # exit 0/1 — probe without reading
vct resolve  --key KEY            # which file would be read (project > shared)
vct exec --secret KEY=ENV -- cmd  # inject into child env (preferred)
vct doctor                        # fix permissions + shape-check github_pat keys
```

NOTE: launcher-managed secrets (`github_pat`, `openai_api_key` registered via
the launcher GUI) live in the OS keychain, NOT here. Those resolve through
vct-hub: `templates/scripts/vct_secrets_resolve.sh <project> <key>` or
`python -c "from vco_lib.agent_secrets import get; ..."`. This directory is
the launcher-independent file store.

## GitHub tokens — which key shape serves which consumer

GitHub issues several token kinds and they are NOT interchangeable. The
classic trap: an App-installation or corrupted long blob stored as
`github_pat` works for `git push` HTTPS but returns `HTTP 401: Bad
credentials` from the `gh` CLI / REST API.

| Key (convention) | Token shape | Length | Serves |
|---|---|---|---|
| `github_pat` | classic PAT `ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}` | 40 | `git push` HTTPS (git-credential-vct), `gh` CLI |
| `GITHUB_TOKEN_FINEGRAINED` | fine-grained PAT `github_pat_…` | ~93 | `gh` REST API with scoped access |
| `github_pat.<suffix>` | any of the above | — | alternates/recovery copies; `vct doctor` shape-checks these too |

Validation patterns (`vct doctor` applies these to every `github_pat`/
`github_pat.*` file and warns on mismatch, without printing values):

- classic: `^ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}$` (exactly 40 chars)
- fine-grained: `^github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]+$` (~93 chars)
- App installation: `^ghs_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}$` — NOT valid for `gh` REST calls
- length sanity: anything 200+ chars under a `github_pat` name is almost
  certainly corrupted (concatenated/duplicated writes) — re-set it.

Trailing-newline gotcha: `vct exec` strips one trailing newline; if you read
a token any other way, strip whitespace before handing it to `gh`:
`GH_TOKEN="$(printf %s "$RAW" | tr -d '\r\n ')"`.

## Other common keys

| Key | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `claude_code_oauth_token` | Claude Code authentication |
| `huggingface_token` | HuggingFace model downloads |
| `openai_api_key` | OpenAI API (only when not launcher/keychain-managed) |

## House rules

- Write via `printf %s "$VALUE" | vct set --project shared --key KEY`
  (never `echo`, never argv).
- Per-project overrides live at `~/.vct-secrets/projects/<NAME>/<key>` and
  win over this directory.
- This file is documentation only — it is skipped by secret resolution and
  safe to edit. Regenerate the shipped baseline by deleting it and re-running
  `python install.py --update`.
